WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.260
Optimization &amp; opportunity cost

2
00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:09.280
Define opportunity cost.

3
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:15.360
The value of the best foregone alternative — used both as a broad idea and to put a dollar value on time.

4
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.860
Why do sunk costs never matter?

5
00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:25.780
They are already spent and unrecoverable. Only future costs and benefits bear on what to do next.

6
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:31.510
Total vs. marginal analysis — why does marginal win?

7
00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:40.480
Same answer, less arithmetic. Keep going while MB ≥ MC and stop where they cross, instead of computing net benefit for every option.

8
00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:44.650
Where is the optimum, exactly?

9
00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:53.920
Where MB and MC cross — not where total benefit is highest and not where cost is lowest. MB falls as you do more; MC usually rises.

10
00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.000
Optimization &amp; opportunity cost — 4 cards
